+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 aimcrazyxx
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+
+"""Procedural materials: stand-in for the package missing from the public source.
+
+Mixar's own ``paint/procedural_materials`` (the backend MatGen library client,
+the sandbox that runs its generated node-group scripts, and the MatGen queue)
+is private, yet a third of the paint module imports it at module scope, so
+without it the layer stack cannot register at all. This fallback keeps the
+same import surface and the standard layers working:
+
+- materials are only those registered at runtime; none are downloaded;
+- a material's script is never executed; only a node group the caller names
+  explicitly, already in the file, is resolved;
+- the backend library reports ``failed`` and MatGen raises, so procedural
+  layers fail closed through their existing error paths.
+"""
+
+PUBLIC_SOURCE_FALLBACK = True
